# tools/probe — Progress (Split 13 rewrite)

Tracks progress converting this package from Check! to Split 13. Tags reflect how much Split-13-specific work each file needs, not whether the current Check! code works. Deliberately outside the root npm workspaces (own manifest) so `npm ci` never pulls a browser into the main install — see design-vault/Architecture/Testing Strategy.md.

Legend: [COMPLETE] no change needed · [IN PROGRESS] being worked on now · [NEEDS WORK] exists, must change/be replaced/repurposed · [MISSING] doesn't exist yet, needs to be created · [WARNING] works but flagged for review · [ERROR] known bug

Updated: 2026-08-30. Update this file in the same pass as any change to a listed file.

- package.json — [COMPLETE]
- package-lock.json — [COMPLETE]
- README.md — [NEEDS WORK] — usage instructions reference Check!'s phases/flags (`--at play --players 2 --seats 6`); update once Split 13's fixed 4-seat flow is built.
- measure.mjs — [WARNING] — generic DOM/viewport measurement helpers likely reusable; verify no Check!-specific selectors.
- viewports.mjs — [COMPLETE] — viewport-matrix definitions, layout-only, game-agnostic.
- player.mjs — [NEEDS WORK] — scripted `socket.io-client` player drives Check!'s specific actions (draw/swap/match/ability); needs Split 13's throw-only action.
- probe.mjs — [NEEDS WORK] — major: drives a full Check! game through its specific stages/phases to sweep layouts; needs rebuilding against Split 13's flow (deal → 13 throw-rounds → hand end) and its fixed 4-seat/2-team layout instead of the 2-6 player matrix.

## Planned / not yet created (Split 13-specific)

- A "sweep the matrix" story for Split 13's fixed 4-seat, 2-team layout (replaces the variable 2-6 player sweep) — [MISSING]
